"http://www.ebi.ac.uk/interpro/entry/IPR047319"},"Title":"['This entry represents the C-terminal domain of DCAF15 (DDB1- and CUL4-associated factor 15), the cullin RING ligase substrate receptor/adaptor that forms a complex with CUL4A or CUL4B, as part of the Rbx-Cul4-DDA1-DDB1-DCAF15 E3 ubiquitin ligase that is responsible for the proteasome degradation of certain proteins [[PMID:31693911], [PMID:31452512]]. Aryl sulfonamide anticancer agents such as indisulam, tasisulam, E7820, and chloroquinoxaline have been shown to recruit the essential mRNA-splic","Publisher":{"Name":"InterPro"}}}]}}]}]}}